From 39c184802b663aede3c9bb0cfd191e16cb620ee5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch <patch@local>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:30:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a bulk selection be moved to one location
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bulk Select could only download. Placement lived entirely on the map
page, behind PlacePicker, which is rendered only when `unplaced.length >
0` and lists unplaced photos exclusively -- so the gallery, which is
where you actually notice that eleven photos from the boat day are
sitting in Sóller, had no way to fix them.

Adds a "Set location" action to the selection tray. It opens a sheet
that offers the same destinations the map does and PATCHes the whole
selection in one request to /api/photos/location, which has always
accepted up to 200 ids and has never been owner-gated: the pin is a fact
about the trip, not about whoever uploaded the file.

The destination list is now shared rather than duplicated. PlacePicker's
"best guess / spots from the trip / trip destinations" sections move out
to DestinationList and PlacePicker renders it, so the two entry points
can't drift apart. Two behaviours are new there and apply to both:

  - Targets are excluded from the clustering. Moving an already-placed
    selection used to be offered "here, where you already are" as the
    first spot, and the time-based guess would suggest a photo's own
    coordinates back to it.
  - The guess and the spot list disable together while a write is in
    flight.

Browse has no map to tap, so "drop a pin instead" hands off to the one
that does: ids go through sessionStorage (200 nanoids is past what a URL
carries reliably) with `?pin=1` as the flag, and the map strips the flag
on arrival so a reload can't drop someone back into pick mode. The map's
"move" prompt is now count-aware, since that path can now carry more
than one photo.

The optimistic update reconciles against the server's `updated` list per
id, matching the map page: a partial write rolls back only the photos
that didn't take, and a total failure throws so the sheet can stay open
and say so.
